Building insighttoolkit5 5.4.7-1+neuro1 (Debian sid)

This is Debian's insighttoolkit5 5.4.7-1 packaging plus two fixes:

1. debian/rules already enables seven ITK remote modules with -DModule_*=ON,
   but also sets -DITK_FORBID_DOWNLOADS=ON and the tree carries only the
   Modules/Remote/*.remote.cmake stubs, so ITK silently skips every one of
   them and the installed package has none. The sources must be present in
   the tree before building. Vendor them into Modules/Remote/<Name>/ (the
   same set, at the ITK-5.4-compatible revisions, as the noble packaging in
   packages/insighttoolkit5):
     GenericLabelInterpolator AdaptiveDenoising
     MorphologicalContourInterpolation GrowCut SimpleITKFilters
     LabelErodeDilate MGHIO IOScanco
   The clean long-term form is one orig-<module>.tar.xz component tarball
   per module (3.0 (quilt) format supports this), which is what should go to
   the Debian maintainer along with the report that the flags are inert.

2. BUILD_TESTING now follows DEB_BUILD_OPTIONS=nocheck instead of being
   forced on: with the remote sources present, the test target of
   MorphologicalContourInterpolation needs the RLEImage remote module,
   which nothing else does.

Build in the sid container with:
  DEB_BUILD_OPTIONS="parallel=4 nocheck" dpkg-buildpackage -us -uc -b
